<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philipp Scheidemann</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philipp Scheidemann was a German Social Democratic politician. On 9 November 1918, the day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a>'s abdication was announced, he proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">German Republic</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> building. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> followed two days later, marking the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philipp-scheidemann.jpg" alt="Philipp Scheidemann" width="311" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1979-122-29A,_Philipp_Scheidemann_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
